e drawled. [179] \"Be serious, Jimmy. This is quite important.\" [180] He walked over to the window and stood there, gazing out. [181] \"Who's Victor King?\" Jimmy asked. \"Another royal family from a Balkan country?\" [182] \"No,\" Anthony said slowly. \"He's not that kind of king.\" [183] \"Then who is he?\" [184] Anthony paused for a moment before saying, \"Jimmy, he's a con artist, a notorious jewel thief, and a brazen one at that. Victor King is just a codename he used in Paris. Paris is his gang's headquarters, and that's where he was caught. But they couldn't find enough evidence for his heavy crimes, so they gave him a light sentence of seven years. He's probably out by now, or maybe already has been.\" [185] \"Do you think Count Stapleton's imprisonment has anything to do with him? Were those thugs following him for revenge?\" [186] \"I don't know,\" Anthony said. \"It doesn't seem like it on the surface. As far as I know, Victor King hasn't touched the Hessian royal family. But it all looks so suspicious, doesn't it? Count Stapleton's death, that memoir, the rumors in the papers \u2013 everything is vague and intriguing. And I've also heard that Hessia has discovered oil. James, I have a strong feeling that they've been eyeing that insignificant little country.\" [187] \"Who?\" [188] \"The Hebrews, the yellow-faced financial moguls sitting in their offices.\" [189] \"So, what's your point?\" [190] \"Just making things complicated, that's all.\" [191] \"Not that,\" Anthony said, slightly disappointed. \"Guess where I'm planning to go with those two hundred and fifty pounds?\" [192] \"South America?\" [193] \"No, I'm going to Hesslovia. I think I could stand with that republic, and maybe even become its president.\" [194] \"Why don't you just claim to be a descendant of the Paulovich bloodline and go there to be a king?\" [195] \"No, James. A king has to reign for life, while a president only serves for four years. For me, a country like Hesslovia, four year