I thought he was talking about a gold mine, then he shoved a small oilcloth package into my hand. Well, I didn't take it seriously at the time. It wasn't until a week later that I opened the package. I admit, I was just too curious. I knew that with Pedro's intelligence, even if he saw a gold mine, he might not recognize it, but what if it was really a gold mine?\" [213] \"The thought of gold must have made your heart race, it's hard to resist,\" Anthony interrupted him. [214] \"I've never felt so disgusted in my life. Gold mine? Ha. For that scumbag, that thing could have been a gold mine. Do you know what it was? A letter from a woman, yes, a British woman. The bitch was blackmailing another woman, and she had the nerve to give me that filthy thing.\" [215] \"Your integrity is admirable, James, but South Europeans are South Europeans. His intentions were good. You saved his life, so he left his livelihood for you.\" [216] \"What am I supposed to do with this thing? Burn it? That's what I thought at first, but then I thought about that poor woman who wouldn't know the letters were destroyed and would be living in constant fear of that South European showing up again.\" [217] \"I never thought you had such an imaginative mind.\" Anthony said, lighting a cigarette, \"You're right, that makes it more complicated. Should we mail it to her?\" [218] \"Like most women, she didn't leave dates or addresses on most of the letters, but there was one with what looked like an address information, but only a name: Chimney Cottage.\" [219] Anthony was about to blow out the match in his hand when he suddenly froze, only to flick it away when the flame burned his fingers. [220] \"Chimney Cottage?\" he said. \"That's too bizarre.\" [221] \"Do you know it?\" [222] \"Darling, it's a British mansion, where the king and queen often spend weekends, and diplomats gather there.\" [223] \"I'd rather you go to England than me, because you know all about these things. I'm just a Canadian coun