ed to wear a gas mask and armor?\" [1934] \"Let's go,\" Bill said. [1935] He slipped on a red satin robe and grabbed a fireplace poker. [1936] \"That's a traditional weapon,\" he said. [1937] \"Let's go,\" Virginia said. \"Be quiet.\" [1938] They tiptoed out of the room, down the corridor, and then down the wide staircase. At the bottom of the stairs, Virginia frowned. [1939] \"Can't your boots be completely silent?\" [1940] \"They're iron nails, after all,\" Bill said. \"I tried my best.\" [1941] \"You need to take them off,\" Virginia said firmly. [1942] Bill grumbled. [1943] \"You can carry them,\" Virginia said. \"I just want to check out the hall. It's so mysterious, Bill. Why would those thieves disassemble that armor?\" [1944] \"Maybe it's just easier to carry in pieces,\" Bill said. \"That's why they disassembled it and put it in the box neatly.\" [1945] Virginia shook her head dissatisfied. [1946] \"Why would they steal an old armor? There are so many valuable things in the chimney house, couldn't they take something easier to carry?\" [1947] Bill shook his head. [1948] \"How many of them were there?\" he asked, gripping the poker in his hand tighter. [1949] \"I couldn't tell, you know how small the keyhole is, and they only had one flashlight.\" [1950] \"I wish they had left by now.\" Bill said hopefully. [1951] He sat on the bottom step of the staircase, taking off his boots. Then, holding one in his hand, he crept down the hallway towards the council chamber. Virginia followed closely behind. They stopped in front of the massive oak door. The room was silent. Virginia nudged Bill's arm, and he nodded. A beam of light appeared in the keyhole, then disappeared. [1952] Bill knelt on the ground, peering through the keyhole. What he saw was hazy, and the obvious action was taking place on the left side of the room, completely out of his line of sight. [1953] The occasional clink of metal could be heard from the room, indicating that the intruders were still r